METHOD
  Started the lead's throwaway instance via serve.sh (full/frozen-live-data
  variant, port 8965, run_in_background — a plain `nohup ... &` inside a
  foreground Bash call is reaped when that call returns, per prior-run
  lesson; confirmed with curl 200 on /dashboard and /static/css/tailwind.css
  before composing anything). GET-fetched all 9 server-rendered pages
  (dashboard/explorer/filemanager/accounts/transfers/duplicates/insights/
  major-expenses/whatif; "/" redirects 307 to /dashboard, confirmed in
  cmd/server/main.go — not a distinct page) plus the HX-Request:true
  fragment for GET /explorer/import/scan (7 entries: 6 identical/disabled +
  1 checked/detected on this frozen data — different mix than IM2's fixture
  variant but same markup shape).
  Composed each page x {light, dark}: forced the real theme class onto
  <html> and neutralized the boot theme-detection script. IMPORTANT: the
  boot script's own HTML COMMENT ("<!-- Theme initialization... -->") is
  stripped by html/template server-side (the documented "don't anchor on
  comments" trap) — my first compose pass anchored on that comment and hit
  0/1 matches on every page; fixed by anchoring the neutralizing regex on
  the actual <script>...localStorage.getItem('theme')... content instead,
  confirmed by grep on the raw fetched HTML before proceeding.
  Spliced the scan fragment into filemanager's #import-scan-list (regex
  innerHTML swap, matching what htmx produces). Opened one major-expenses
  row (Amazon, 358 matched txns) by setting its tbody's data-open="true" and
  the toggle button's aria-expanded="true" — the exact attribute pair
  internal/../major-expenses.js's setRowOpen() sets client-side; the detail
  <tr> (a real <table> of matched transactions, A-7) is server-rendered
  already, CSS-only hidden via `tbody[data-open="false"] > tr.detail-row
  {display:none}`, so this reproduces the opened state faithfully without
  executing page JS (tracing, not running, per this lane's job).
  Added <base href="http://127.0.0.1:8965/"> so absolute /static/... paths
  resolve against the live instance's real built stylesheet.
  Ran `npx @axe-core/cli` (v4.13.0) with --tags wcag2a,wcag2aa,wcag22aa on
  all 18 composed files.
  HARNESS BUG CAUGHT AND DISCARDED: the first parallel batch used a
  *relative* `file://$f` path per invocation; Chrome/axe silently resolved
  that to its own internal error page (host="composed" is not a valid
  file:// authority) and reported an IDENTICAL bogus 1-violation
  "meta-viewport / user-scalable=no" on all 18 outputs — the reported
  offending <meta> HTML (`maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no`) does not
  exist anywhere in raw/ or composed/ output (verified by grep), which is
  what exposed it as a harness artifact rather than a real defect. Re-ran
  with `file://$(pwd)/...` (absolute paths) and got materially different,
  self-consistent results — those are what this verdict is based on.

